# Design craft

D-024 in `docs/DECISIONS.md` is the visual baseline. The idea of "jump" is forward movement: the logo, a teal mark, and a colored word in a headline. No bouncing graphics.

## Do not default to

- Blue-purple gradient heroes, glowing blobs, glassmorphism, circuit or robot imagery
- Equal three-column service cards, fake metric rows, logo walls, or testimonial strips
- The same card treatment on every section, or a giant closing CTA band on every page
- Scroll hijacking, custom cursors, or entrance motion on every block

## Require

- The first screen says what Jump does: technology services, managed IT, and business advisory.
- Change composition between sections. Type and whitespace carry the brand.
- Teal `#00DED8` is for marks and the closing button, not small text. Emphasized words use blue `#0174AD`. Body text uses navy `#021639`.
- DM Sans for UI and body. Poppins for headlines. One italic blue word per headline is enough.
- Motion needs a purpose. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Target WCAG 2.2 AA.
- Design 375px layouts on purpose. Do not only stack the desktop page.

If a section still works after swapping in another company name, redesign it. Detail is in `docs/BRAND_DIRECTION.md`.

```tsx
// Wrong: a generic services grid
<section className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-6">{services.map(Card)}</section>

// Right: one editorial index, each row a different weight of type and detail
<ol>{services.map(ServiceIndexRow)}</ol>
```
